  ($q$cs-55$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Words in Context$q$, 2, $q$The artisan's papermaking technique remained ______ despite decades of industrial automation elsewhere, as she still pulled each sheet by hand from a wooden frame.$q$, $q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?$q$, $q$["traditional","mechanized","obsolete","digital"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Pulling each sheet by hand from a wooden frame, despite automation elsewhere, describes a traditional technique, not a mechanized or digital one.$q$),
  ($q$cs-56$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$An essay on the Silk Road opens by listing the goods that traveled along it — silk, spices, glassware — then argues that ideas and technologies, not just objects, moved along the same routes, and spends its remaining paragraphs tracing how papermaking techniques spread westward this way.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?$q$, $q$["To broaden a narrow view of the Silk Road as only a route for physical goods","To argue that the Silk Road carried no physical goods at all","To provide a complete inventory of every good traded historically","To criticize papermaking as an inferior technology"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The essay starts with goods, then explicitly argues for a broader view that includes ideas and technologies, matching choice A's description of the purpose.$q$),
  ($q$cs-57$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Perfumer A argues that synthetic fragrance compounds can replicate natural scents so precisely that trained noses cannot reliably tell the difference in blind tests.

